<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  four_way_crossing — hand-authored for osc2r2 (see maps/README.md).

  One four-arm junction with all 12 movements, and four arms that lead away from
  it: a straight climb west, a clothoid bend north, a poly3 offset east, a plain
  straight south. Drawn in the map's own local frame; there is deliberately no
  <geoReference>, the map is not a copy of any real place.

  Every arm's s axis points away from the junction, so lane -1 always leaves the
  junction and lane +1 always enters it. Geometry element anchors are chained,
  and each turn is a quarter circle of radius 10 m, which is exactly the distance
  from the junction centre to an arm (tests/maps.rs pins that the connecting
  roads land on their arm with no kink).

-->
<OpenDRIVE>
  <header revMajor="1" revMinor="7" name="four_way_crossing" version="1.0" date="2026-09-04" north="179.035246973" south="-138.0" east="148.0" west="-168.0" vendor="osc2r2"/>
  <!-- West arm. Flat through the junction, then a 2.5 m climb away from it. -->
